<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best World Drop Items for Frost Death Knights</span></h2>Mists of Pandaria brings with it a whole lot of world content with the chance to get powerful gear. This includes Rare Mobs, like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50352/qunas">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Qu'nas</span></a>, but also World Bosses, such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=60491/sha-of-anger">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sha of Anger</span></a>.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="sha-of-anger">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Sha of Anger</span></h3>Sha of Anger is notable in that it drops item level 496 Tier 14 Legs and Gloves, as well as various item level 483 Malevolent Gladiator's pieces. This is a great way to get a headstart on your Tier set if you get lucky. <br/>
<br/>The first time you kill the Sha of Anger, it will also drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89317/claw-of-anger">
<img alt="Claw of Anger" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_hand_1h_shaclaw.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Claw of Anger</span></a>. This can be turned in for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90912/angerforged-stompers">
<img alt="Angerforged Stompers" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Angerforged Stompers</span></a>, a decent early pair of boots.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="rare-mobs">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Rare Mobs</span></h3>There are tons of Rare mobs scattered around Pandaria, and each one has their own unique drop. Most of these are toys, cosmetics, or similar items, but a small handful can drop strong equipment. None of these items are likely to last you until raiding, but they can be a great stepping stone when gearing in pre-raid content.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=51078/ferdinand">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ferdinand</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50823/mister-ferocious">
