<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Frost Death Knights</span></h2>Mists of Pandaria offers a handful of powerful crafted items early on, which you should look out for. Some are profession specific, while other items are BoE and therefore available on the Auction House. Some of these items will only see use for a short while, while others have much greater longevity and will essentially be used for the entirety of the phase.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> can only be crafted and used by Engineers and is the most powerful helmet available prior to Celestial Dungeons and the Mogu'shan Vaults raid. The high item level gives it a high amount of base stats, and the two Cogwheel Sockets offer an incredible amount of flexibility where you can obtain a large amount of both Hit and Expertise if required.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is your best-in-slot  trinket for all of Phase 1, which makes it a high priority to obtain t. It will likely be expensive, as it requires multiple daily cooldowns from a character with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a>. You can either craft this yourself, use an alt character, or buy it from the Auction House if you have the gold.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82975/ghost-reavers-breastplate">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Breastplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Breastplate</span></a> is your best available chest prior to Mogu'shan Vaults and Celestial Dungeons. It requires the expensive crafting material <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=72104/living-steel">
<img alt="Living Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ingot_livingsteel.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Living Steel</span></a>, which comes from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82976/ghost-reavers-gauntlets">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets</span></a> - As with the chest, these gloves are your best available item prior to later content releasing, and they also requires Living Steel.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Frost Death Knights Trinkets</span></h2>As a Frost Death Knight you generally want trinkets that yield the highest amount of Strength possible, as this is your most precious Stat due to multiple modifiers.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Frost Death Knights typically want two passive trinkets, as they can be used in conjunction with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>, granting the highest amount of Strength possible.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a> is not the greatest trinket but is still a powerful early option and has the added bonus of only costing Valor Points. It has a high amount of passive Strength, which is nice. The fact that its active effect is Haste also makes it less punishing to use as an Engineer.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a> has a powerful on-use effect with a large amount of Strength. The added passive Expertise is nice for early gearing.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is generally the best passive trinket until you have obtained your Heroic Raid BiS. It has passive Strength and a large proc that also grants Strength. While it is likely to be very expensive early on, this trinket is so incredibly powerful that you should make it your highest priority to obtain.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> is a good placeholder until better trinkets come your way. The passive Strength and powerful Crit proc makes it a great early option.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is a bit of an outsider trinket. It is the best trinket you can get until you obtain Celestial or Raid-trinkets, due to its powerful Strength proc. It does require you to become an Alchemist, so you need to decide if you want to sacrifice a profession to obtain this item, which won't see use for more than a few weeks at most.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> has one of our much-beloved Strength procs as well as a large amount of passive Haste, which we're generally short on in Phase 1.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> has passive Strength and a large Haste proc but won't see use until you have the Heroic version.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Frost Death Knights</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the  <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<div data-inserted-ad-group="2" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
<div data-ad="inline-leaderboard" data-multiformat="true" id="ad_inline-leaderboard_2" style="width: 728px; height: 250px; background: rgba(136, 136, 136, 0.133); --ad-width: 728px; --ad-height: 250px;">
<div data-house-ad="true" data-house-show-before-ad-request="" style="width: 728px; height: 90px;">
<a href="https://tidd.ly/4ckL1JD" target="_blank">
<img alt="ad" src="//r2.rev.iq/wowhead.com/House_BlizzGear_Apparel_728x90.webp"/></a></div></div></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might. <br/>
<br/>It is even more important to be Hit capped as a Frost Death Knight, since both your Summoned Ghoul and Army of the Dead inherit your Hit chance and will miss if not capped.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will however still be able to parry them. For the vast majority of raid bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry attacks from behind.<br/>
<br/>Expertise also grants Spell Hit in Mists of Pandaria, making it much more important than earlier. Since a large part of your skill kit is spell-based, not missing is essential.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Frost Death Knights</span></h2>Frost Death Knight has always been a class that feels better with gear. The more Crit and Mastery you have, the more fun your character is to play. Gems are also a great place to grab any Hit and Expertise that we may be missing. This can be especially useful when aiming for Socket Bonuses, as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76643/senseis-wild-jade">
<img alt="Sensei's Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sensei's Wild Jade</span></a> is typically a good way to utilize a Blue Socket if we want the bonus.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76696/bold-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Bold Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76671/keen-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Keen Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Keen Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76684/etched-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Etched Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Green Gems</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76643/senseis-wild-jade">
<img alt="Sensei's Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sensei's Wild Jade</span></a></div></li>
<li>
